<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">bounty</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">bounty</ansi> command lets you view open bounties posted by
factions and quest-givers. Fulfilling a bounty earns gold and
reputation with the issuing faction.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bounty list</ansi> [<ansi fg="yellow">filter</ansi>]
    List open bounties. Optional filter:
      <ansi fg="yellow">mob</ansi>                 only bounties on creatures
      <ansi fg="yellow">player</ansi>              only bounties on players
      <ansi fg="yellow"><faction-slug></ansi>       only bounties from that faction
                           e.g. <ansi fg="command">bounty list thornwall_guards</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bounty show</ansi> <ansi fg="yellow"><id></ansi>
    Show full detail of a single open bounty.

<ansi fg="yellow">Examples:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bounty list</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">bounty list mob</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">bounty list thornwall_guards</ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">bounty show 3</ansi>

Notice boards in guard barracks and constabulary offices also
display current postings in-fiction.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help faction</ansi>
